AC = \sqrt{AB^2 + BC^2} = \sqrt{6^2 + (3\sqrt{3})^2} = \sqrt{36 + 27} = \sqrt{63} = 3\sqrt{7}
\] The median $CN$ to the hypotenuse is half the length of the hypotenuse $AC$. So, the length of $CN$ is \[
CN = \frac{3\sqrt{7}}{2}
\] Since $P$ is the centroid, it divides the median $CN$ into a ratio of 2:1, so \[
CP = \frac{2}{3} \times CN = \frac{2}{3} \times \frac{3\sqrt{7}}{2} = \sqrt{7}
\] The length of $CP$ is $\sqrt{7}$. </think> <answer> $\sqrt{7}$ </answer>

